UID:james-castle-house-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T211016Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Deadline: James Castle House: 2027 Artist Residencies (Boise\, Idah
 o)
DESCRIPTION:The James Castle House in Boise\, Idaho (the preserved home of 
 self-taught artist James Castle) opens applications for its 2027 residency
  terms from 16 July to 28 August 2026. TWO-MONTH RESIDENCY: an immersive f
 ocus on a project or body of work responding to the history and legacy of 
 James Castle or the site\; open to artists\, scholars\, creators and profe
 ssionals in any field\; $4\,000 stipend\; residents share their practice t
 hrough public events (workshops\, open studios\, presentations) and donate
  a selected piece to the City of Boise collection. Terms: 1 March - 30 Apr
 il\, 1 June - 31 July\, or 1 September - 31 October 2027. TWO-WEEK RESIDEN
 CY: time and space for a single site-responsive project\; $1\,000 stipend\
 ; one public event. Terms: 11-25 January or 1-15 December 2027. A rolling 
 PROJECT RESIDENCY also considers proposals case by case (email jamescastle
 house@cityofboise.org). ELIGIBILITY: 18+\, legally able to work in the Uni
 ted States\, able to pass a background check\; emerging and mid-career pra
 ctitioners in any field\, though the property cannot accommodate loud or e
 specially messy processes. Residents live alone on site. Selection by comm
 ittee on strength of proposal\, application\, work samples and references.
  Virtual information session 21 July 2026\, 1pm MT. Applicants notified Se
 ptember 2026. DEADLINE: 28 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: James Castle Hous
 e / City of Boise\nLocation: Boise\, Idaho\, USA. Open to applicants legal
 ly able to work in the United States.\nAward: $4\,000 stipend for two-mont
 h terms or $1\,000 for two-week terms\, to assist with living expenses and
  supplies\, plus solo live-in accommodation and studio at the historic Jam
 es Castle House. Residents donate one selected piece to the City of Boise 
 collection at the end of the term. No application fee.\nDuration: Two-mont
 h terms (1 Mar - 30 Apr\, 1 Jun - 31 Jul\, 1 Sep - 31 Oct 2027) or two-wee
 k terms (11-25 Jan and 1-15 Dec 2027)\n\nMore: https://www.jamescastlehous
 e.org/residencies/apply/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
URL:https://www.jamescastlehouse.org/residencies/apply/?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Boise\, Idaho\, USA. Open to applicants legally able to work in th
 e United States.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:modern-art-oxford-micro-commissions-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T211016Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260726
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260727
SUMMARY:Deadline: Modern Art Oxford: Collaborative Micro-commissions Open C
 all 2026
DESCRIPTION:Modern Art Oxford marks its 60th anniversary with an open call 
 for three collaborative micro-commissions responding to the question: how 
 can collective practice/s help us to embrace uncertainty and complexity? C
 ollectives\, duos\, partnerships and collaborative groups based across the
  South East of England are invited to propose new small-scale experimental
  works for a group exhibition in the Ground Floor Gallery\, running alongs
 ide a major solo exhibition by Mike Nelson\, who is also on the selection 
 panel. Proposals may take the form of multidisciplinary research\, site-re
 sponsive work\, grassroots organising\, performance\, visual art\, sound\,
  poetry or other creative practices\; ideas should respond to the theme of
  collective practice and uncertainty\, explore collaborative approaches\, 
 experiment across disciplines\, be achievable within the budget and timeli
 ne\, and be original to this open call (building on existing research is f
 ine). WHO: groups of two or more people\, including established artist col
 lectives\, newly formed collaborations\, interdisciplinary partnerships\, 
 informal or community-led groups\, and family collaborations\, based in th
 e Arts Council England South East area (Oxfordshire\, Berkshire\, Buckingh
 amshire\, Hampshire and Isle of Wight\, Surrey\, Kent\, East Sussex\, West
  Sussex). SUPPORT: each of the three selected collectives receives a GBP 1
 \,000 artist fee\, up to GBP 500 production budget\, curatorial mentorship
 \, four months of exhibition display\, installation photography\, promotio
 n\, technical and production support\, and transport support within the So
 uth East. TIMELINE: online briefing and Q&A 15 June 2026 (email creativele
 arning@modernartoxford.org.uk for the link)\; selection confirmed 14 Augus
 t 2026\; production August to November 2026\; preview party 4 December 202
 6\; exhibition 5 December 2026 to April 2027. Apply via Google Forms\; an 
 information pack PDF and FAQ are on the call page. DEADLINE: Sunday 26 Jul
 y 2026\, 23:59.\n\nOrganisation: Modern Art Oxford\nLocation: Oxford\, UK.
  Open to collectives\, duos\, partnerships and collaborative groups based 
 in the Arts Council England South East area (Oxfordshire\, Berkshire\, Buc
 kinghamshire\, Hampshire and Isle of Wight\, Surrey\, Kent\, East Sussex\,
  West Sussex).\nAward: GBP 1\,000 artist fee per selected collective\, plu
 s up to GBP 500 production budget\, curatorial mentorship from the Modern 
 Art Oxford team\, four months of public exhibition display\, professional 
 installation photography\, promotion\, technical and production support\, 
 artwork transport support within the South East\, peer networking\, and in
 clusion in a public preview event. No application fee.\nDuration: Producti
 on August to November 2026\; install 23 November to 4 December 2026\; exhi
 bition 5 December 2026 to April 2027\n\nMore: https://modernartoxford.org.
 uk/blog/open-call-2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://modernartoxford.org.uk/blog/open-call-2026?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Oxford\, UK. Open to collectives\, duos\, partnerships and collabo
 rative groups based in the Arts Council England South East area (Oxfordshi
 re\, Berkshire\, Buckinghamshire\, Hampshire and Isle of Wight\, Surrey\, 
 Kent\, East Sussex\, West Sussex).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:avistavulcao-azores-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T211016Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260801
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260802
SUMMARY:Deadline: AVISTAVULCÃO: Azores Artist Residency 2027 (Faial\, Port
 ugal)
DESCRIPTION:AVISTAVULCÃO opens a call for a one-month artist-in-residence 
 programme focused on research and creation\, taking place in March 2027 an
 d intended for an artist or artistic duo. Located on the island of Faial n
 ear the Capelinhos Volcano (Azores\, Portugal)\, the residency offers imme
 rsion in a territory shaped by geology\, insularity\, and the interplay be
 tween nature and human presence\, with the Azores treated as living materi
 al for creation. Artists are invited to develop projects engaging with lan
 dscape\, memory\, local history\, and the contemporary challenges facing p
 eripheral regions\; suggested starting points include geological time\, tr
 ansformation\, resilience\, isolation\, mobility\, and the relationships b
 etween communities and the environment. Context-sensitive proposals that p
 rioritise observation\, listening and a relationship with the place are va
 lued. Residents meet local stakeholders and share moments with the communi
 ty\, culminating in a public presentation of the process or results. SUPPO
 RT (in-person mobility): EUR 1\,350 allowance per resident\, travel allowa
 nce of EUR 400 to 800\, green mobility top-up of EUR 400\, visa top-up of 
 EUR 120 per resident\, outermost regions top-up of EUR 175 per resident\, 
 family top-up of EUR 200 per child\, and accessibility support. ELIGIBILIT
 Y: individual artists and duos (cross-disciplinary welcome) from countries
  eligible for the Creative Europe programme. DEADLINE: 1 August 2026.\n\nO
 rganisation: AVISTAVULCÃO / Barca 13\nLocation: Faial Island\, Azores\, P
 ortugal (near the Capelinhos Volcano). Open to artists from countries elig
 ible for the Creative Europe programme.\nAward: EUR 1\,350 allowance per r
 esident for the month\, plus travel allowance (EUR 400 to 800)\, green mob
 ility top-up (EUR 400)\, visa top-up (EUR 120/resident)\, outermost region
 s and overseas territories top-up (EUR 175/resident)\, family top-up (EUR 
 200 per child/resident)\, and accessibility support. No application fee.\n
 Duration: One month\, March 2027\n\nMore: https://www.barca13.pt/en/avista
 vulcao/agora/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.barca13.pt/en/avistavulcao/agora/?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Faial Island\, Azores\, Portugal (near the Capelinhos Volcano). Op
 en to artists from countries eligible for the Creative Europe programme.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jcal-artworks-fellowship-2026-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T211016Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260713
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260714
SUMMARY:Deadline: JCAL: ARTWorks Fellowship 2026-2027
DESCRIPTION:Jamaica Center for Arts and Learning (JCAL) invites New York Ci
 ty-based visual artists to apply for ARTWorks\, its Artist Fellowship Trai
 ning Seminar Series: a six-month fellowship focused on career sustainabili
 ty that amplifies the work of emerging\, underrepresented visual artists. 
 Six Fellows treat their practice as a small business\, set entrepreneurial
  and professional goals\, and build a long-term plan\, supported by a Prog
 ram Manager\, an established Artist Mentor\, cohort meetings\, and at leas
 t six seminar events (past topics: copyright and contracts\, working with 
 galleries and collectors\, grant writing\, taxes and accounting\, marketin
 g\, art handling). SUPPORT: $5\,000 per Fellow paid over the program\, fre
 e shared studio space (about 550 sq ft\, as available) with a storage clos
 et\, one free JCAL class\, and a concluding two-month group exhibition wit
 h catalogue (opens 9 April 2027). ELIGIBILITY: reside in New York City (pr
 eferably Queens) or Long Island\; identify as BIIPOC (Black\, Immigrant\, 
 Indigenous\, People of Color)\; demonstrate clarity of concept and strong 
 craft with a deep commitment to social practice\; must NOT have received m
 ajor exposure via exhibitions\, grants or residencies\; must not be enroll
 ed in any college degree or certificate program\; past Fellows ineligible.
  Priority to Queens-based artists of underrepresented communities\; multid
 isciplinary practices welcome\, but the program focuses on visual artists 
 working in traditional forms. APPLY via Submittable with six images OR two
  3-5 minute videos\, a one-page work-sample description\, artist statement
  (max 300 words)\, one professional reference (max 300 words)\, CV\, and a
  paragraph on your expectations of ARTWorks. Jury reviews submissions with
 out obvious identifiers. TIMELINE: first-round notifications 3 August 2026
 \, interviews 11-14 August\, Fellows notified 21 August\, program runs 7 O
 ctober 2026 to 18 June 2027. DEADLINE: midnight Monday 13 July 2026 (porta
 l closes 14 July 2026\, 6:00 AM ET).\n\nOrganisation: Jamaica Center for A
 rts and Learning (JCAL)\nLocation: Jamaica\, Queens\, New York City\, USA.
  Open to visual artists based in New York City (preferably Queens) or Long
  Island\; priority to Queens-based BIIPOC artists.\nAward: $5\,000 per Fel
 low\, paid out over the course of the program\, plus free shared studio sp
 ace at JCAL (about 550 sq ft\, as available)\, a 7 x 4 ft storage closet\,
  one free JCAL class (space-available)\, an Artist Mentor and seminar seri
 es\, and a concluding two-month group exhibition with catalogue in JCAL's 
 Miller and Community galleries. No application fee.\nDuration: Six-month f
 ellowship: 7 October 2026 to 18 June 2027\; exhibition opens 9 April 2027\
 n\nMore: https://jcal.submittable.com/submit/354501/artworks-fellowship-20
 26-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://jcal.submittable.com/submit/354501/artworks-fellowship-2026-202
 7?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Jamaica\, Queens\, New York City\, USA. Open to visual artists bas
 ed in New York City (preferably Queens) or Long Island\; priority to Queen
 s-based BIIPOC artists.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
