UID:larose-osler-library-artist-in-residence-2026-2027@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T211016Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: Michele Larose - Osler Library Artist-in-Residence 2026-2
 027
DESCRIPTION:Annual artist-in-residence award funded by Dr. Michele Larose\,
  hosted by the Osler Library of the History of Medicine at McGill Universi
 ty\, supporting visual artists who use McGill collections to create works 
 addressing contemporary and/or historical subjects in medicine and the hea
 lth sciences. Possible projects include painting\, photography\, performan
 ce\, sculpture\, and digital\, video or installation art. Most work is ant
 icipated to be inspired by Osler Library collections\; sources may also in
 clude other McGill Libraries\, the Maude Abbott Medical Museum\, and McGil
 l faculties and hospitals. NO STUDIO SPACE provided\; the library offers r
 esearch support\, research space\, and exhibition space. RESIDENCY DUTIES:
  work on the project\; give a public presentation\; exhibit or perform the
  work\; submit a report suitable for the Osler Library Newsletter\; comple
 te the work by 30 April 2027. The artist retains ownership of the work but
  must credit Dr. Larose and the Osler Library. Applicants are encouraged t
 o propose a project engaging one of the Faculty of Medicine and Health Sci
 ences Strategic Research Plan themes: Infection (as a threat)\; Cancer (as
  a complex global challenge)\; The Brain\; or Personalized/ing medicine. E
 LIGIBILITY: degree in Studio Arts or a related field and/or a history of e
 xhibiting work in professional venues\; open to non-Canadians\, but prefer
 ence typically given to Montreal-based or easily-traveling artists. APPLY 
 by emailing ONE PDF (filename: lastname.LaroseOsler2026.pdf) to awards.osl
 erlibrary@mcgill.ca containing a 1-page project description\, proposed tim
 eline\, CV\, one letter of recommendation (addressed to Head Librarian Dr.
  Mary Hague-Yearl)\, and work samples (typically 5-15 images). Reference l
 etters may also be sent separately by the referee before the deadline. Res
 ults announced in August or September. Deadline: 31 July 2026.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Osler Library of the History of Medicine\, McGill University (funded
  by Dr. Michele Larose)\nLocation: Montreal\, Quebec\, Canada (open to all
 \; preference typically given to artists who reside in or can easily trave
 l to Montreal)\nAward: $6\,000 CAD (taxes may be deducted)\; paid in two p
 arts (half at the beginning of the residency\, half on completion). Covers
  travel\, materials\, and related expenses. No application fee.\nDuration:
  Research component flexible (2-3 weeks\, consecutive or spread out) betwe
 en October 2026 and April 2027\; all work must be completed and the exhibi
 tion ready to open by 30 April 2027\n\nMore: https://www.mcgill.ca/librari
 es/locations/osler/awards/artist-residence?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mcgill.ca/libraries/locations/osler/awards/artist-residence
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Montreal\, Quebec\, Canada (open to all\; preference typically giv
 en to artists who reside in or can easily travel to Montreal)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aerowaves-twenty27@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T211016Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260715
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260716
SUMMARY:Deadline: Aerowaves Twenty27: Call for Emerging European Choreograp
 hers
DESCRIPTION:Aerowaves selects 20 emerging choreographers based in geographi
 cal Europe each year (the Twenty27 cohort) to have their work presented at
  the Spring Forward festival (14-17 April 2027 in Limerick\, Ireland) and 
 at many of Aerowaves' partners around Europe\; Aerowaves promotes the sele
 cted artists for a year\, creating performance opportunities with partners
 . EVERY APPLICANT (selected or not) has the chance to be programmed by Aer
 owaves network partners\; around 100 performance opportunities per year ar
 e supported by Aerowaves. ELIGIBILITY: applicants must be resident in geog
 raphical Europe\; due to the Russian invasion of Ukraine\, Aerowaves partn
 ers do NOT accept applications of works made in Russia or Belarus. ONE wor
 k per applicant per year. The work must have been produced in geographical
  Europe\; must be 15-40 minutes\; must be finished and have been presented
  to the public (a studio sharing counts\; work-in-progress or rehearsal fo
 otage does NOT). The work should be easily included in a double or triple 
 bill with simple technical requirements\; works created for public/non-con
 ventional spaces and outdoors are welcome. WHAT SELECTED ARTISTS GET: pres
 entation fee at Spring Forward plus travel (within Europe)\, hotel and per
  diem/hospitality for each team member\; a year of Aerowaves website promo
 tion. DEADLINE: 15 July 2026. APPLY via the Aerowaves how-to-apply page.\n
 \nOrganisation: Aerowaves (Spring Forward festival hosted in Limerick\, Ir
 eland)\nLocation: Festival in Limerick\, Ireland (14-17 April 2027) plus p
 artner venues across Europe\; applicants must be resident in geographical 
 Europe\nAward: For presentation at Spring Forward: a fee plus expenses inc
 luding travel within Europe\, hotel and a per diem/hospitality for each te
 am member. Around 100 partner performance opportunities are guaranteed eac
 h year and supported by Aerowaves. Selected applicants additionally receiv
 e a year of Aerowaves promotion (artist profile\, images\, video\, press c
 overage). No application fee.\nDuration: One year of Aerowaves promotion a
 nd partner-network presentations\; presentation at Spring Forward 14-17 Ap
 ril 2027\n\nMore: https://aerowaves.org/artists/how-to-apply/?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://aerowaves.org/artists/how-to-apply/?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Festival in Limerick\, Ireland (14-17 April 2027) plus partner ven
 ues across Europe\; applicants must be resident in geographical Europe
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pioneer-works-visual-arts-music-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20260904T211016Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260717
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260718
SUMMARY:Deadline: Pioneer Works: 2027 Open Call – Visual Arts and Music R
 esidency (Brooklyn\, NY)
DESCRIPTION:Pioneer Works in Red Hook\, Brooklyn invites applications from 
 emerging visual artists and musicians for its 2027 residency cohort. 12 Vi
 sual Arts residents (5-month residency) and 12 Music residents (1-month re
 sidency) are selected each year through a two-phase jury process. WHAT IS 
 PROVIDED: free studio space\; access to facilities including risograph pri
 nter\, darkroom\, ceramics studio\, large-format printer\, 3D printers\, t
 hermobinder\, and laser cutter\; biweekly studio visits with curators\, ga
 llerists\, critics\, and artists\; free access to all public programmes at
  Pioneer Works\, including Second Sundays (monthly open studios and perfor
 mances). FINANCIAL AWARD: USD 5\,000 for Visual Arts residents\; USD 3\,00
 0 for Music residents (each comprising a USD 2\,500 honorarium plus USD 50
 0/month for the residency duration)\; applicants' choice on how to spend i
 t. Pioneer Works does not provide housing\, travel\, or visa sponsorship. 
 ELIGIBILITY: open locally\, nationally\, and internationally\; collectives
  may apply (resources shared)\; current students and programme alumni are 
 not eligible. REVIEW PROCESS: phase one is internal scoring on technical a
 bility\, uniqueness of vision\, and future potential (nontraditional caree
 r paths given special consideration)\; highest scorers advance to an exter
 nal jury of art professionals and alumni who assess diversity of demograph
 ics and media\, genuine studio need\, and fit with Pioneer Works' public-f
 acing culture. Jury convenes September 2026\; all applicants notified by l
 ate September. Supported by Dalio Philanthropies\, the Andy Warhol Foundat
 ion\, NYC Department of Cultural Affairs\, New York State Council on the A
 rts\, and the National Endowment for the Arts. APPLY: via Pioneer Works we
